The shell acts on the same system as the graphical desktop---same files,
only the interface varies (\cref{sec:shell,sec:filesystem}).
A file made in the file manager and a listing typed in the shell meet in
the same directory.
The correct answer expects the file to appear; the distractor that keeps
the two interfaces apart is the undiscerned-aspect case, that a student
expects the shell and the graphical view to show different files.

